        <definition>bool StrNCmpInliner::optimizeStrNCmp</definition>
        <argsstring>()</argsstring>
        <name>optimizeStrNCmp</name>
        <qualifiedname>anonymous_namespace{AggressiveInstCombine.cpp}::StrNCmpInliner::optimizeStrNCmp</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>First we normalize calls to strncmp/strcmp to the form of compare(s1, s2, N), which means comparing first N bytes of s1 and s2 (without considering &apos;\0&apos;). </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Examples:</para>
<para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">strncmp(s,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;a&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/>3)<sp/>-&gt;<sp/><ref refid="namespacellvm_1_1_scaled_numbers_1a0651aa0a52c69c4fe12cf730e7ed65ab" kindref="member">compare</ref>(s,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;a&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/>2)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">strncmp(s,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;abc&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/>3)<sp/>-&gt;<sp/>compare(s,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;abc&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/>3)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">strncmp(s,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;a\0b&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/>3)<sp/>-&gt;<sp/>compare(s,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;a\0b&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/>2)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">strcmp(s,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;a&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">)<sp/>-&gt;<sp/>compare(s,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;a&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/>2)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">char</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>s2[]<sp/>=<sp/>{</highlight><highlight class="charliteral">&apos;a&apos;</highlight><highlight class="normal">}</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">strncmp(s,<sp/>s2,<sp/>3)<sp/>-&gt;<sp/><ref refid="namespacellvm_1_1_scaled_numbers_1a0651aa0a52c69c4fe12cf730e7ed65ab" kindref="member">compare</ref>(s,<sp/>s2,<sp/>3)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">char<sp/>s2[]<sp/>=<sp/>{</highlight><highlight class="charliteral">&apos;a&apos;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="charliteral">&apos;b&apos;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="charliteral">&apos;c&apos;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="charliteral">&apos;d&apos;</highlight><highlight class="normal">}</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">strncmp(s,<sp/>s2,<sp/>3)<sp/>-&gt;<sp/><ref refid="namespacellvm_1_1_scaled_numbers_1a0651aa0a52c69c4fe12cf730e7ed65ab" kindref="member">compare</ref>(s,<sp/>s2,<sp/>3)</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para>We only handle cases where N and exactly one of s1 and s2 are constant. Cases that s1 and s2 are both constant are already handled by the instcombine pass.</para>
<para>We do not handle cases where N &gt; StrNCmpInlineThreshold.</para>
<para>We also do not handles cases where N &lt; 2, which are already handled by the instcombine pass. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
